as you've been since you got together.

256
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:24,380
Do you really wanna throw that all away over a room?

257
00:13:24,550 --> 00:13:26,840
That is so silly.

258
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:30,640
What's more important, love...

259
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:32,310
or silliness?

260
00:13:33,930 --> 00:13:36,810
Well, we are fond of the silliness.

261
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:39,400
But we also have a soft spot for the love.

262
00:13:40,310 --> 00:13:42,820
Love is the best medicine.

263
00:13:40,310 --> 00:13:42,820
That's laughter.

264
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,900
Why do you do it?

265
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,900
I don't know.

266
00:13:49,530 --> 00:13:53,870
Now, Chandler, you wanna live with Monica, right?

267
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,540
Yeah, I do.

268
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:59,040
And, Mon, you wanna live with Chandler, don't you?

269
00:13:59,250 --> 00:14:00,380
Yes.

270
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:04,210
Good. A verbal contract is binding in the state of New York.

271
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:16,720
So I understand you're looking for a place?

272
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:21,350
No, no, I'm staying put.

273
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:21,350
Oh.

274
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:26,480
I was going to offer you my apartment.

275
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,240
Why? Where are you going?

276
00:14:30,410 --> 00:14:31,780
I don't know.

277
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,910
Hey, Rach.

278
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,910
Hi.

279
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:40,370
Uh, you're never gonna believe it. Monica and Chandler are moving in again.

280
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:44,000
That's great news, right? I mean, for them, right?

281
00:14:44,590 --> 00:14:45,880
Oh, wow.

282
00:14:46,050 --> 00:14:49,170
But on the bright side, we get to be roommates again.

283
00:14:49,970 --> 00:14:53,550
Yeah. You know, about that, um...

284
00:14:54,350 --> 00:14:59,310
Ross, ahem, I really appreciate your offer to let me move in and everything...

285
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,440
but don't you think it's gonna be weird?

286
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:07,320
Why? Why? Why would it...? Why would it be weird?

287
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:10,400
Well, you know, because of us.

288
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,490
Because of our history.

289
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:14,870
No.

290
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:14,870
No?

291
00:15:15,030 --> 00:15:17,080
No, no.

292
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:20,500
It would only be weird if we were still in that place.

293
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:24,330
I mean, are you still in that place?

294
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:27,750
No, not at all.

295
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:27,750
Good. Me neither.

296
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,550
So it's not a problem.

297
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:33,090
We're just two friends who happen to be roommates.

298
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:36,600
Okay, but, Ross, eventually, you and I are gonna be dating.

299
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:41,680
Really? We are?

300
00:15:41,850 --> 00:15:45,270
Well, yeah. I'm gonna have a boyfriend and you're gonna have a girlfriend.

301
00:15:46,270 --> 00:15:47,860
Oh. Heh.

302
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:50,690
That'd be great.

303
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:54,280
But if you think it's gonna be okay, we'll just work out a system.

304
00:15:54,450 --> 00:15:57,950
It'll be like in college. I'll hang a hanger on the door and put a sign:

305
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:00,160
"Come back later. I'm getting lucky."

306
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:09,300
Yeah, I didn't think of that.

307
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:15,220
So are you sure about this whole moving-in thing?

308
00:16:15,390 --> 00:16:20,310
I mean, it's a really big step. And what's the rush?

309
00:16:23,850 --> 00:16:25,350
That's very funny.

310
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:28,310
He's being silly because he knows we enjoy the silliness.

311
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:33,570
No, I'm serious, okay? I mean, think about it.

312
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:38,160
You move in, you start fighting over stupid game rooms...

313
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:40,080
next thing you know, you break up.

314
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:43,450
Ross, you were right before. It was just a stupid fight about a room.

315
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:45,210
Okay, there are no stupid fights.

316
00:16:46,750 --> 00:16:48,790
This isn't about the room.

317
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:52,510
This is about what the room represents.

318
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:56,880
And unfortunately, this room could destroy you.

319
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:00,720
Yeah, I'm not so worried.

320
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:00,720
Yeah, no, me neither.

321
00:17:00,890 --> 00:17:03,390
Fine. It's your life.

322
00:17:04,270 --> 00:17:05,940
I just don't wanna see you break up.

323
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:10,020
Which you will do if you move in together.

324
00:17:12,570 --> 00:17:15,490
But if that's what you want, there's nothing I can do.

325
00:17:15,650 --> 00:17:17,660
Don't do it!

326
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:25,040
You still wanna move in together, right?

327
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:25,040
Of course.

328
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:26,620
Ross didn't scare you?

329
00:17:26,790 --> 00:17:29,380
Scared me out of ever wanting to live with him.

330
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:33,590
Come here, I gotta show you something.

331
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:33,590
Okay.

332
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:38,180
Oh, my God, someone's killed Square Man.

333
00:17:40,970 --> 00:17:42,970
This is where the Barcalounger could go.

334
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:46,730
You see, you can see the TV, and still, it's walking distance to the kitchen.

335
00:17:46,890 --> 00:17:49,690
Oh, that's so sweet.

336
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,230
I wanna show you something.

337
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:54,820
You know those big road signs that say "merge"?

338
00:17:55,070 --> 00:17:56,400
Mm-hm.

339
00:17:56,570 --> 00:17:58,990
You know? So I was thinking we could get one of those signs...

340
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,280
and hang it over our bed.

341
00:18:02,330 --> 00:18:05,080
Because that's you and I together.

342
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,410
"Merge."

343
00:18:08,290 --> 00:18:10,250
Oh, my God, I love that.

344
00:18:08,290 --> 00:18:10,250
Really?

345
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:12,170
"No."

346
00:18:15,090 --> 00:18:18,340
I found you in my bed

347
00:18:18,510 --> 00:18:21,180
How'd you wind up there?

348
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:24,350
You are a mystery

349
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:29,980
Little black curly hair

350
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:33,150
Little black, little black Little black, little black

351
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:38,240
Little black curly hair

352
00:18:39,610 --> 00:18:41,280
Thank you.

353
00:18:42,030 --> 00:18:43,660
Um...

354
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:46,540
If you wanna receive e-mails about my upcoming shows...

355
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:50,250
then please give me money so I can buy a computer.

356
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,460
So, uh... Ahem.

357
00:18:55,630 --> 00:18:57,550
Where are the other guys?

358
00:18:57,710 --> 00:19:00,170
Well, let's see, Monica and Chandler are occupied.

359
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,930
Fighting?

360
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,930
No, the other thing.

361
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:06,060
I really think it's great they worked things out.

362
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:09,060
Yeah, there's no breaking them up, is there?

363
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:13,060
Hey, can I borrow the key to your house so I can make a copy?

364
00:19:13,230 --> 00:19:15,730
Here.

365
00:19:13,230 --> 00:19:15,730
Thank you.

366
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:16,940
Now, are you sure?

367
00:19:17,110 --> 00:19:20,240
Because once I make a copy, there's no turning back.

368
00:19:20,990 --> 00:19:22,070
Yeah, I'm sure.

369
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:25,950
Now get out of here before I change my mind.

370
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:32,080
Uh, listen, Ross.

371
00:19:32,250 --> 00:19:35,170
You really think this moving in with Rachel is a good idea?

372
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:37,800
I've been back and forth.

373
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:41,170
Yeah, well, maybe you should go back, okay?

374
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:43,300
Rachel moves in, and before you know it...

375
00:19:43,470 --> 00:19:45,850
you're where you don't wanna be, back together.

376
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:47,510
Yeah, I don't think so.

377
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:50,350
She's already talking about, you know, dating other guys.

378
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:51,850
That's not gonna work out.

379
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:55,400
Then she's gonna come home all weepy, and you'll be telling her:

380
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,610
"Oh, that's okay. You'll find someone."

381
00:19:57,770 --> 00:20:00,990
And then, bam, she finds you.

382
00:20:03,030 --> 00:20:05,530
Huh. Oh, maybe you're right.

383
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:09,200
I am telling you, Ross, she is definitely gonna fall in love with you again.

384
00:20:09,370 --> 00:20:10,660
Now, is that what you want?

385
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:14,420
Heh. Is that what I want?

386
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:14,420
Yes.

387
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:19,880
Here she comes. I'm gonna make your life much easier.

388
00:20:20,050 --> 00:20:23,010
All right, well, the place was closed, so I'll copy it later.

389
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,380
Or not.

390
00:20:24,590 --> 00:20:27,140
Uh, Rach, why don't you just move in with me?

391
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:28,680
Ahh.

392
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:28,680
Oh.

393
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:32,020
Whoa, whoa, Joey.

394
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:32,020
No, no, no. It's okay.

395
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:37,520
Look, Rach, I know I scared you off with that whole naked-Thursdays thing...

396
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,940
but we don't have to do that.

397
00:20:41,570 --> 00:20:45,110
Well, it would be easier to move just right across the hall.

398
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:49,830
Wait a minute, unless you're thinking about naked Wednesdays.

399
00:20:50,830 --> 00:20:53,580
Thursday's clearly not good for you. Pick a day.

400
00:20:59,710 --> 00:21:00,750
Hi.

401
00:20:59,710 --> 00:21:00,750
Hi.

402
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:03,510
Come on in. Thanks for coming back.

403
00:21:03,670 --> 00:21:06,300
Okay, there have been a lot of people interested in the room.

404
00:21:06,470 --> 00:21:09,300
But I have narrowed it down, and you are one of the finalists.

405
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:11,970
Great.

406
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:11,970
Okay, now, before I make my decision...

407
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:15,350
I just wanna make sure that our personalities match, okay?

408
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:16,810
So I made up a little test.

409
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:21,070
Now, I'm gonna say a word, and then you say the first thing that comes to mind.

410
00:21:21,230 --> 00:21:23,940
I can do that.

411
00:21:21,230 --> 00:21:23,940
Okay, here we go.

412
00:21:24,110 --> 00:21:25,530
Pillow.

413
00:21:24,110 --> 00:21:25,530
Fight.

414
00:21:25,990 --> 00:21:27,530
Very good.

415
00:21:28,410 --> 00:21:30,660
Okay. G.

416
00:21:30,830 --> 00:21:32,990
String?

417
00:21:30,830 --> 00:21:32,990
Excellent.

418
00:21:34,540 --> 00:21:36,580
Okay. Um...

419
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:38,830
Doggy.

420
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:43,250
Kitten?

421
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:43,250
Ooh, sorry.

422
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:48,130
No, no, no. So close, though. But, you know, okay, bye-bye.

